<title>USA: Diamond Cable sells $250 mln in zero coupon bonds.</title>
<headline>Diamond Cable sells $250 mln in zero coupon bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following $250 million issue from Diamond Cable Communications Plc was priced on Friday in a 144a offering via Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The deal was increased to $250 million from an original size of $175 million due to strong investor demand, sources said.</p>
<p>BORROWER DIAMOND CABLE COMMUNICATIONS PLC</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	COUPON 10 3/4 PCT MATURITY 2/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE SNR DISC NTS ISS PRICE 59.448  FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/02 LAST MOODY'S B3   YIELD 10 3/4 PCT  PAY FREQ BEGINS PAYING</p>
<p>						CASH SEMI-ANNUALLY ON</p>
<p>						8/15/02</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS  SPREAD N/A	  CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE IN</p>
<p>							   FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1662</p>
